WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.789 --> 00:00:05.990
Speaker 1: Yesterday, I didn't even get to
this because we were so busy with other stories,

00:00:05.990 --> 00:00:08.850
but this is a pretty big story.

00:00:08.850 --> 00:00:12.870
Prosecutors in charge of the Trump criminal
probe have resigned.

00:00:12.870 --> 00:00:15.809
They have resigned.

00:00:15.809 --> 00:00:21.800
The Associated Press reporting the two prosecutors
in charge of the Manhattan District Attorney's

00:00:21.800 --> 00:00:28.470
criminal investigation into Trump and his
business dealings suddenly resigned on Wednesday,

00:00:28.470 --> 00:00:33.890
throwing the future of the probe into question
just as pressure was building on Trump.

00:00:33.890 --> 00:00:35.480
A spokesperson for D.A.

00:00:35.480 --> 00:00:41.710
Alvin Bragg confirmed the resignations of
Carrie Dunn and Mark Pomerantz, two top deputies

00:00:41.710 --> 00:00:44.990
who had been tasked with running the investigation
day to day.

00:00:44.990 --> 00:00:47.390
They started on the probe under former D.A.

00:00:47.390 --> 00:00:54.330
Cyrus Vance and stayed on done, the office's
former general counsel argued before the Supreme

00:00:54.330 --> 00:00:58.650
Court in a successful multiyear fight for
Trump's tax records.

00:00:58.650 --> 00:01:05.210
Pomerantz is a former mafia prosecutor brought
out of private practice to add expertize in

00:01:05.210 --> 00:01:10.810
white collar investigations and has been questioning
witnesses before the grand jury.

00:01:10.810 --> 00:01:14.390
Bragg spokesperson Danielle Wilson said We
are grateful for their service and didn't

00:01:14.390 --> 00:01:18.240
say anything else, indicating the investigation
is ongoing.

00:01:18.240 --> 00:01:24.680
But of course, many people saying, OK, the
investigation is ongoing, but it is basically

00:01:24.680 --> 00:01:25.680
over.

00:01:25.680 --> 00:01:27.280
It is basically over.

00:01:27.280 --> 00:01:31.690
And now the right is saying this is proof
the investigation was bogus.

00:01:31.690 --> 00:01:36.630
What the right wants you to believe is that
the investigation into Trump was meritless

00:01:36.630 --> 00:01:41.480
and bogus, and in protest, these two investigators
quit.

00:01:41.480 --> 00:01:43.799
There is no evidence of that.

00:01:43.799 --> 00:01:46.280
There's just no evidence of that.

00:01:46.280 --> 00:01:53.200
What we do know with certainty is that there
is major hesitation right now from any prosecutor

00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:55.340
to actually charge Trump.

00:01:55.340 --> 00:02:02.600
So if we want to speculate, a much more reasonable
speculation would be the resignation is because

00:02:02.600 --> 00:02:09.009
the investigators realize no matter what happens,
Trump's not getting charged and they were

00:02:09.009 --> 00:02:12.760
sick of doing work that they feel will be
in vain.

00:02:12.760 --> 00:02:18.970
Again, I'm saying, if we want to speculate,
that's way more likely that there's evidence

00:02:18.970 --> 00:02:23.579
against Trump, and the investigators realized
this was never going to charge.

00:02:23.579 --> 00:02:26.200
What the hell are we doing here wasting our
time?

00:02:26.200 --> 00:02:27.810
But both are mere speculation.

00:02:27.810 --> 00:02:32.029
We don't actually know that either of those
is the reason, and so we can only wait and

00:02:32.029 --> 00:02:34.069
see if we get a comment.

00:02:34.069 --> 00:02:35.879
That being said?

00:02:35.879 --> 00:02:41.079
As I've said before, I don't think Trump's
ever going to see a day of prison, and I don't

00:02:41.079 --> 00:02:47.260
think these resignations contradict what is
meant by my position on this for a very, very

00:02:47.260 --> 00:02:48.790
long time years at this point.

